                <td>£80,000</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Second Round (Last 16)</strong></td>
                <td><strong>£10,000</strong></td>
                <td>£5,000</td>
                <td>8</td>
                <td>£80,000</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Group Stage Runners-up (2nd)</strong></td>
                <td><strong>£6,000</strong></td>
                <td>£3,000</td>
                <td>12</td>
                <td>£72,000</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Group Stage Third Place (3rd)</strong></td>
                <td><strong>£5,000</strong></td>
                <td>£2,500</td>
                <td>12</td>
                <td>£60,000</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="table-total">
                <td><strong>Total Tournament Purse</strong></td>
                <td>—</td>
                <td>—</td>
                <td><strong>40</strong></td>
                <td><strong>£500,000</strong></td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>
          To see how this £500,000 purse compares with solo ranking majors like the World Championship and World Matchplay, explore our comprehensive guide to <a href="/tournament/prize-money/">PDC tournament prize money</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 5: Venue -->
      <section class="content-card">
        <h2>Venue: Eissporthalle, Frankfurt</h2>
        <p>
          Since 2022, the World Cup of Darts has established a permanent home at the <strong>Eissporthalle in Frankfurt, Germany</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Known for its lively arena atmosphere and cavernous seating bowl, the Eissporthalle regularly welcomes thousands of passionate European darts supporters across four days of summer action. The 2026 championship took place from 11 to 14 June 2026, generating packed sessions and deafening support for home and visiting nations alike.
        </p>
        <p>
          The German venue has proven an ideal European hub for international supporters, providing convenient rail and air connections for fans travelling from across the UK, Netherlands, Belgium, and Scandinavia.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 6: How to Watch -->
      <section class="content-card">
        <h2>How to Watch the World Cup of Darts</h2>
        <p>
          The World Cup is broadcast live across global television networks and digital streaming platforms:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>United Kingdom &amp; Ireland:</strong> Broadcast live on Sky Sports Arena and Sky Sports Main Event, with streaming available via the Sky Go and NOW apps.</li>
          <li><strong>Germany, Austria &amp; Switzerland:</strong> Streamed live and on-demand through DAZN.</li>
          <li><strong>Netherlands:</strong> Broadcast live on Viaplay.</li>
          <li><strong>Rest of the World:</strong> Streamed internationally through PDCTV for subscribers outside the UK, Germany, and the Netherlands.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          For complete broadcast schedules, country-by-country channel listings, and streaming tips, visit our comprehensive <a href="/watch/">where to watch darts</a> broadcasting directory.
        </p>
      </section>

